From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] prf-long final: D4 (the multi-message bound at l(n)-bit
 outputs) and the re-derivations

D4 (new module Encryption/PrivateKey/FromPRF/MultiMsgOut.lean): encodeTupleOut with its reader,
MultiMsg.encodeList_eq_flatMap (the public general form of FromPRF.lean's private lemma, which
stays), encodeTupleOut_eq_flatten and MultiMsg.exists_negligible_distAdv_prfEncRealOut.
FromPRF.lean imports it; the bridge encodeTuple_eq_encodeTupleOut; encodeTuple_eq_flatten and
prfScheme_multiMessageSecure re-derived as the case l = var. Encryption/PrivateKey.lean: one
import and one Contents bullet. ReductionMachine.lean: encodeHist_eq_flatMap is now the term
encodeHist_eq_flatMapOut h (no funext; axioms back to [propext]). No frozen header or
definition changes.
